StickerForge's application code is MIT. See LICENSE and NOTICE.md.

The Windows package includes the official Node.js Windows x64 runtime. The
complete Node.js and bundled component license text travels with the application
as engine/Node-LICENSE.txt. Runtime source:
https://nodejs.org/dist/v24.19.0/node-v24.19.0.tar.gz

The Node sidecar includes Baileys, pino, qrcode, qrcode-terminal and their
production dependencies. See each module's license in engine/node_modules.
The application frontend uses React (MIT), Lucide (ISC and MIT) and Tauri APIs
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). Their notices and the Rust dependency notices are included
in engine/notices. The lockfiles identify the exact dependency sources.

FFmpeg and FFprobe are fetched directly from Gyan by the optional in-app setup.
They are distributed by Gyan under GPL terms for that build. The setup verifies
the fixed archive's SHA-256 and installs its license alongside the executables.
https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/

yt-dlp (Unlicense, with separate third-party terms in bundled variants) is
supported by the legacy command-line downloader and is not distributed in the
desktop installers.
